        "original_id": "ffa9168d-c5ed-54c7-964b-48955faa7b66",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dennis Locorriere, Maja Ivarsson, Sev Lewkowicz, Toril Lindqvist, Tim Smit, Sarah Miles, Jeff Duff, Tony Clarke\n- Bands and Projects: Dr. Hook & the Medicine Show, Dr. Hook, The Sounds, Mungo Jerry, Any Trouble, Guano Apes, She's a Machine!, We Are Rebels, Open Your Eyes\n\nFacts:\n- Dennis Locorriere was born on June 13, 1949, in Union City, New Jersey, United States.\n- Dennis Locorriere is an American former lead vocalist and guitarist of Dr. Hook & the Medicine Show, later known as Dr. Hook.\n- Maja Ivarsson was born on October 2, 1979.\n- Maja Ivarsson is a Swedish singer and the lead vocalist of the Swedish indie rock band The Sounds.\n- Sev Lewkowicz has played and recorded with Mungo Jerry, Dennis Locorriere, Any Trouble, Tim Smit, Sarah Miles, Jeff Duff, and Tony Clarke.\n- The North American CD release of She's a Machine! includes a cover of the Guano Apes song \"Open Your Eyes\".\n- The North American CD release of She's a Machine! includes a single edit of \"We Are Rebels\" in which Maja Ivarsson's guest vocals were removed and sung instead by Toril Lindqvist.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
